# Applies to every build in docker-compose.prod.yml, because they all use
# the repo root as their context (`web` joined them — see CLAUDE.md §13c).
#
# This file is not a size optimisation, it is load-bearing. Without it,
# `COPY apps/web/ ./` in apps/web/Dockerfile.prod copies the HOST's
# apps/web/node_modules straight over the node_modules installed in the
# deps stage — replacing a Linux install with whatever the developer's
# machine happens to have, including native binaries built for the wrong
# platform. It also kept ~1.3 GB of node_modules and .next out of the
# build context that would otherwise be uploaded to the daemon on every
# build.
#
# Only things no Dockerfile here needs are listed. apps/api/Dockerfile.prod
# copies exactly `apps/api` and `packages/transcoder`; apps/web's copies
# `apps/web` and `packages/design-tokens`. Nothing below is inside those
# beyond generated output.

# Dependencies — always reinstalled inside the image, never copied in.
**/node_modules

# Build output
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
apps/desktop/dist

# Generated into the desktop renderer by scripts/sync-*.js at predev/
# prebuild time; not part of any image.
apps/desktop/src/renderer/tokens.css
apps/desktop/src/renderer/icons.js
apps/desktop/src/renderer/logo.svg

# Python bytecode and local virtualenvs
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv

# VCS and editor noise
.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea

# Local env / secrets. .env.prod is supplied to containers via env_file at
# RUN time, and must never be baked into an image layer.
.env
.env.*
**/.env.local

# Tests and docs that no runtime image needs
**/.pytest_cache
**/coverage
